⍝ IBM APL2 ⎕AV, row by row, as character literals: ⎕UCS shows which code
⍝ point each character of a literal arrives as (GNU APL vs. IBM APL2 via
⍝ the MEGA11 harness, i.e. through testcases_apl2/apl2_codec.py). Control
⍝ characters, DEL, | and ⋸ cannot be in a literal here and are left out,
⍝ and so are ⍬ ⍶ ⍹: they are not in IBM APL2's real ⎕AV (verified with
⍝ ⎕UCS 16 16⍴⎕AV below), although GNU APL's table of it has them.

